00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:57.770
And our question this week
has to do with Cloud Build.

00:28:57.770 --> 00:29:00.210
And the question is, how do
you cache files between builds

00:29:00.210 --> 00:29:02.460
in Cloud Build, which is
something that a lot of folks

00:29:02.460 --> 00:29:04.290
want to do to speed
up their builds and/or

00:29:04.290 --> 00:29:06.120
because they've got interesting
pipelines that they're

00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:08.745
trying to build where they have
lots of different dependencies.

00:29:08.745 --> 00:29:11.233
So, Mark, what is the
answer to this question?

00:29:11.233 --> 00:29:12.900
MARK MANDEL: I had
exactly this problem.

00:29:12.900 --> 00:29:14.422
Basically, I had
a file-based case

00:29:14.422 --> 00:29:16.380
that I wanted to store
some records in and just

00:29:16.380 --> 00:29:18.770
persist it between builds
to make things a bit faster.

00:29:18.770 --> 00:29:21.990
And I was like, OK, clearly,
I have Google Cloud Storage.

00:29:21.990 --> 00:29:24.120
I can push stuff up and down.

00:29:24.120 --> 00:29:25.500
But what if it's not there?

00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:26.310
What if it is?

00:29:26.310 --> 00:29:27.880
I don't want to
write all this code.

00:29:27.880 --> 00:29:30.400
So I went hunting
through the repository,

00:29:30.400 --> 00:29:32.400
which is the Cloud
Builders Community

00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:34.560
Repository under Google
Cloud Platform, which

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:37.985
has a bunch of Google
Cloud Builder steps.

00:29:37.985 --> 00:29:39.360
Now, these are
custom-build steps

00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:41.400
that you can use yourself
inside Cloud Build that

00:29:41.400 --> 00:29:42.520
do some kind of fancy things.

00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:43.690
And there's a whole
bunch of them.

00:29:43.690 --> 00:29:44.590
I'm not going to go
through them all.

00:29:44.590 --> 00:29:47.007
But one of them that stands
out and one that I really like

00:29:47.007 --> 00:29:49.560
is there is a cache
build step, or a cache,

00:29:49.560 --> 00:29:52.020
depending on whether you're
Australian or American.

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:54.360
And what it has, it has a
safe cache and a restore cache

00:29:54.360 --> 00:29:54.943
functionality.

00:29:54.943 --> 00:29:57.360
So it will take basically
any path that you like

00:29:57.360 --> 00:29:59.220
and check it in
Google Cloud Storage.

00:29:59.220 --> 00:30:00.315
You can have keys.

00:30:00.315 --> 00:30:01.940
You can have your
own keys if you want.

00:30:01.940 --> 00:30:03.982
You can tell it what bucket
you want to put into.

00:30:03.982 --> 00:30:06.160
It will even do checksumming
of a particular file.

00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:07.380
So if you want the
cache to be stored

00:30:07.380 --> 00:30:08.790
within the checksum
of a file and you

00:30:08.790 --> 00:30:10.530
want it to change
when the file change,

00:30:10.530 --> 00:30:12.310
it's all kind of baked
in and just works.

00:30:12.310 --> 00:30:13.920
So if you're looking
for that, we'll

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:15.175
put a link in the show notes.

00:30:15.175 --> 00:30:16.050
But it's super handy.

00:30:16.050 --> 00:30:16.650
I just put it in.

00:30:16.650 --> 00:30:17.180
It just worked.

00:30:17.180 --> 00:30:17.490
It was great.

00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:17.730
AJA HAMMERLY: Yeah.

00:30:17.730 --> 00:30:20.010
And that whole community,
all those community

00:30:20.010 --> 00:30:22.530
supply builders are really
great because, oftentimes,

00:30:22.530 --> 00:30:24.447
the problems we have are
problems someone else

00:30:24.447 --> 00:30:25.420
